1
00:00:28,720 --> 00:00:29,980
He's running out of mana!

2
00:00:29,980 --> 00:00:31,610
Don't get your hopes up.

3
00:00:32,360 --> 00:00:36,310
Even if my Archer-class ability to sustain my life reaches its limits,

4
00:00:36,680 --> 00:00:39,720
given the vast difference in our fighting abilities,

5
00:00:39,720 --> 00:00:41,570
it won't even prove to be a handicap.

6
00:00:42,340 --> 00:00:43,780
And, Emiya Shirou...

7
00:00:44,430 --> 00:00:47,530
it doesn't change the fact that you're going to die.

8
00:00:57,610 --> 00:01:01,380
Rin, I will take your heart.

9
00:01:02,790 --> 00:01:05,920
Kotomine, this isn't what we agreed on!

10
00:01:05,920 --> 00:01:08,510
You said you'd give Tohsaka to me!

11
00:01:08,510 --> 00:01:10,270
S-Stop!

12
00:01:10,270 --> 00:01:11,350
You can't have Tohsaka!

13
00:01:14,370 --> 00:01:18,350
Do you have any last words?

14
00:01:19,640 --> 00:01:21,800
I will grant any final request of yours.

15
00:01:23,580 --> 00:01:28,600
You should already know exactly
what's going through my head right now.

16
00:01:28,600 --> 00:01:30,070
True.

17
00:01:30,070 --> 00:01:33,040
Not giving up until the bitter end is your hallmark, Rin.

18
00:01:33,780 --> 00:01:35,420
But what makes you remarkable

19
00:01:35,420 --> 00:01:40,380
is that at the same time you realize
you cannot change what is about to happen.

20
00:01:42,250 --> 00:01:43,590
I admire that.

21
00:01:43,590 --> 00:01:46,970
That contradiction is exquisite.

22
00:02:04,610 --> 00:02:07,070
Lancer... You...

23
00:02:07,940 --> 00:02:10,140
I hate to break it to you, Kotomine,

24
00:02:10,890 --> 00:02:15,830
but I wouldn't be much of a hero if this was enough to kill me.

25
00:02:27,490 --> 00:02:28,760
Damn it all.

26
00:02:30,670 --> 00:02:32,900
So things ended up like this anyway, huh?

27
00:02:32,900 --> 00:02:33,990
Talk about stupid.

28
00:02:43,130 --> 00:02:46,820
"The Holy Grail is yours," my ass!

29
00:02:50,070 --> 00:02:53,330
Once useless, always useless, I suppose.

30
00:02:53,610 --> 00:02:54,790
Isn't that right, holy man?

31
00:02:56,360 --> 00:02:59,870
But I won't make a fuss.

32
00:02:59,870 --> 00:03:02,440
I don't hold a grudge over your actions.

33
00:03:03,130 --> 00:03:06,630
And speaking ill of the dead is unseemly.

34
00:03:07,030 --> 00:03:09,290
Sorry to keep you waiting, Tohsaka!

35
00:03:09,850 --> 00:03:13,760
We've had all kinds of interruptions,
but it's finally just the two of us.

36
00:03:14,020 --> 00:03:18,680
I can't have you going and dying on me that easily.

37
00:03:18,680 --> 00:03:22,770
It wouldn't be fair to me, not after I've been so patient, right?

38
00:03:22,970 --> 00:03:26,500
The Holy Grail is as good as mine!

39
00:03:26,500 --> 00:03:28,510
You still have time, you know.

40
00:03:28,510 --> 00:03:32,780
If you agree to be mine, I might even share it with you.

41
00:03:33,500 --> 00:03:34,900
Good grief.

42
00:03:36,600 --> 00:03:38,870
Have you not learned your lesson?

43
00:03:39,640 --> 00:03:40,670
Don't you get it?

44
00:03:40,670 --> 00:03:43,380
You're the one who still has time, you idiot!

45
00:03:43,380 --> 00:03:46,540
If you don't want to die, get out of here right now!

46
00:04:07,400 --> 00:04:09,930
Grovel for me, Tohsaka!

47
00:04:09,930 --> 00:04:14,380
If I like what I hear, I might just spare your life!

48
00:04:14,380 --> 00:04:17,310
I swear, your stupidity defies all reason.

49
00:04:17,310 --> 00:04:19,520
I'll warn you one last time.

50
00:04:19,520 --> 00:04:21,410
Get out of here right now!

51
00:04:22,320 --> 00:04:24,080
Is that all you have to say?

52
00:04:24,670 --> 00:04:27,630
Who's gonna stop me, huh?!

53
00:04:30,490 --> 00:04:32,030
Stupid kid.

54
00:04:32,030 --> 00:04:35,020
You aren't worthy to touch that woman.

55
00:04:36,010 --> 00:04:37,490
Excuse me?

56
00:04:37,490 --> 00:04:40,930
The dead man walking has a bone to pick?

57
00:04:43,740 --> 00:04:46,770
I'm not gonna let you die painlessly, got it?

58
00:04:47,650 --> 00:04:49,770
Hey, that's your cue, Gilgamesh!

59
00:04:49,770 --> 00:04:52,610
This guy says he wants a hero's death!

60
00:04:55,200 --> 00:04:56,500
Hey.

61
00:04:56,500 --> 00:04:58,780
Come on... What the hell is he doing?

62
00:04:59,150 --> 00:05:00,460
Aren't you listening?

63
00:05:00,460 --> 00:05:02,910
I said to get your ass over here!

64
00:05:08,650 --> 00:05:09,880
Damn it.

65
00:05:10,480 --> 00:05:12,710
Stupid kid made me waste energy.

66
00:05:12,710 --> 00:05:15,130
Thanks. You saved my life.

67
00:05:16,620 --> 00:05:18,650
Well, it just worked out that way.

68
00:05:19,230 --> 00:05:21,330
You don't owe me any thanks.

69
00:05:23,800 --> 00:05:24,780
Lancer!

70
00:05:32,360 --> 00:05:33,530
Crap!

71
00:05:53,190 --> 00:05:56,840
Did you really think your projections were on the same level as mine?

72
00:05:57,370 --> 00:06:00,370
While you may mimic the appearance and material features of the original,

73
00:06:00,370 --> 00:06:03,100
if the structure isn't logically sound, it's worthless.

74
00:06:04,400 --> 00:06:06,480
Damn it!

75
00:06:32,280 --> 00:06:33,350
Now I get it.

76
00:06:33,350 --> 00:06:35,110
That explains why you're so tough.

77
00:06:35,110 --> 00:06:38,810
I've heard of magic that enables you to master old skills

78
00:06:38,810 --> 00:06:42,620
by communing with selves from past lives
and letting them possess you.

79
00:06:42,620 --> 00:06:46,770
It appears that every time our swords clash,
your skills are being honed.

80
00:06:46,770 --> 00:06:48,380
No kidding?

81
00:06:48,380 --> 00:06:50,730
Then I guess we're both copycats.

82
00:06:50,730 --> 00:06:52,490
Keep talking tough.

83
00:06:52,490 --> 00:06:54,610
I'll catch up to you soon enough!

84
00:06:54,990 --> 00:06:56,980
Catch up to me?

85
00:06:56,980 --> 00:06:58,850
You have it completely wrong.

86
00:06:58,850 --> 00:07:02,110
You truly don't understand anything.

87
00:07:02,110 --> 00:07:03,200
What do I have wrong?

88
00:07:05,510 --> 00:07:09,620
Your belief that you ever had the slightest chance of winning!

89
00:07:29,390 --> 00:07:32,530
This is how it all ended for him?

90
00:07:34,460 --> 00:07:36,090
I don't feel sorry for him.

91
00:07:36,630 --> 00:07:38,270
I don't feel sorry for him.

92
00:07:38,940 --> 00:07:40,670
I don't feel sorry for him!

93
00:07:41,740 --> 00:07:42,790
But...

94
00:07:43,670 --> 00:07:47,750
When I think that my feet will be taking me down his path,

95
00:07:47,750 --> 00:07:49,480
my heart feels like it will break.

96
00:07:50,990 --> 00:07:53,010
When I see what you believed in—

97
00:07:53,010 --> 00:07:55,190
what you believe in—

98
00:07:55,190 --> 00:08:00,060
is nothing but a pipe dream wrapped in lies,

99
00:08:00,060 --> 00:08:01,260
I...

100
00:08:06,180 --> 00:08:07,430
Shirou!

101
00:08:08,440 --> 00:08:13,520
Judging by that pathetic expression that says you're about to vomit,

102
00:08:14,150 --> 00:08:15,510
you saw it, didn't you?

103
00:08:16,690 --> 00:08:18,910
That simplifies things, then.

104
00:08:18,910 --> 00:08:22,450
Everything you saw is true, Emiya Shirou.

105
00:08:23,110 --> 00:08:26,000
That's what "catching up to me" will get you.

106
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:27,960
You should see it once more, with your own eyes.

107
00:08:29,080 --> 00:08:31,790
The world where I ended up.

108
00:08:32,330 --> 00:08:35,850
I am the bone of my sword.

109
00:08:35,850 --> 00:08:37,550
Unknown to Death.

110
00:08:37,550 --> 00:08:39,050
Nor known to Life.

111
00:08:40,050 --> 00:08:43,180
Unlimited Blade Works!

112
00:08:58,290 --> 00:08:59,620
Don't worry about me.

113
00:09:00,650 --> 00:09:02,640
I'm used to this.

114
00:09:03,750 --> 00:09:09,240
Dying because of some dumb order comes with being a hero.

115
00:09:09,820 --> 00:09:14,750
Man, I guess we both got stuck with crappy partners, huh?

116
00:09:15,030 --> 00:09:16,570
You're right.

117
00:09:16,570 --> 00:09:22,160
But I think mine was more "unruly" than "crappy."

118
00:09:22,160 --> 00:09:23,450
That's for sure.

119
00:09:24,120 --> 00:09:27,690
Most humans are a pain in the ass,

120
00:09:27,690 --> 00:09:30,510
but that guy takes the cake.

121
00:09:31,170 --> 00:09:33,690
So he was too much, even for you?

122
00:09:33,690 --> 00:09:36,890
Yes, but that's what motivated me.

123
00:09:37,470 --> 00:09:40,230
As long as Archer was my Servant,

124
00:09:40,230 --> 00:09:45,700
I swore to myself that I'd only do what I thought was right.

125
00:09:45,970 --> 00:09:49,200
I hate to say it, but I can't save him.

126
00:09:50,070 --> 00:09:52,380
Because I think he's right.

127
00:09:53,240 --> 00:09:55,870
His choices, his regret over them...

128
00:09:55,870 --> 00:09:58,170
I think they're all justified.

129
00:09:58,170 --> 00:10:02,850
I'm so dispassionate when it comes to that stuff that I even anger myself.

130
00:10:03,710 --> 00:10:07,180
So all I can do is focus on myself.

131
00:10:07,940 --> 00:10:12,930
Just like a certain someone once did,
I'll keep going down the path I believe in.

132
00:10:13,280 --> 00:10:15,370
That's the only example I can set.

133
00:10:16,480 --> 00:10:21,560
That's about all I could do to repay him.

134
00:10:24,710 --> 00:10:28,990
I'd have no complaints with a woman like you as a partner,

135
00:10:29,340 --> 00:10:33,110
but I never did have any luck at finding good women.

136
00:10:33,110 --> 00:10:33,990
Damn it all.

137
00:10:34,520 --> 00:10:38,150
I guess that'll never change, no matter how many tries I have.

138
00:10:40,120 --> 00:10:42,070
You'd better get going.

139
00:10:42,070 --> 00:10:43,830
I'll take him with me.

140
00:10:49,230 --> 00:10:51,050
Goodbye, Lancer.

141
00:10:51,050 --> 00:10:55,190
I didn't know you long, but I like people like you.

142
00:11:00,260 --> 00:11:01,510
Silly girl.

143
00:11:02,370 --> 00:11:05,320
Come see me again when you have a few more years on you.

144
00:11:18,110 --> 00:11:21,890
The foolishness of appearing here, knowing you're no match for me...

145
00:11:21,890 --> 00:11:27,650
You're a sham who's never had a goal of his own, obsessed with a stupid ideal his entire life.

146
00:11:27,650 --> 00:11:30,520
Is it finally clear that's who you really are?

147
00:11:31,620 --> 00:11:36,510
The need to save people simply because you want to is a faulty emotion.

148
00:11:37,380 --> 00:11:42,410
You're fundamentally broken as a human being—
a fake that should never have existed.

149
00:11:42,410 --> 00:11:45,320
Such a life holds no value at all.

150
00:11:46,610 --> 00:11:48,970
I am your ideal.

151
00:11:48,970 --> 00:11:52,070
It should be clear by now that you're no match for me.

152
00:12:00,790 --> 00:12:02,240
I see.

153
00:12:02,240 --> 00:12:05,050
Your refusal to accept me is only natural.

154
00:12:05,760 --> 00:12:08,470
As long as I am your ideal,

155
00:12:08,470 --> 00:12:11,970
you, Emiya Shirou, must reject me more than anyone.

156
00:12:21,000 --> 00:12:22,830
Then let me ask you.

157
00:12:22,830 --> 00:12:26,650
Do you really want to become a champion of justice?

158
00:12:27,490 --> 00:12:29,190
You're asking me that now?

159
00:12:29,820 --> 00:12:32,350
I don't want to become one.

160
00:12:32,350 --> 00:12:34,900
I will become one!

161
00:12:36,800 --> 00:12:37,550
Yes.

162
00:12:38,160 --> 00:12:40,790
You must become one, no matter what.

163
00:12:40,790 --> 00:12:42,540
And that is because...

164
00:12:42,540 --> 00:12:45,750
it is the only emotion Emiya Shirou possesses.

165
00:12:46,030 --> 00:12:50,770
Even if it isn't something that comes from within himself.

166
00:12:52,960 --> 00:12:56,330
From your reaction, it seems like you have always suspected it.

167
00:12:57,110 --> 00:13:00,170
I no longer remember much of my past.

168
00:13:00,800 --> 00:13:04,420
But nevertheless, I remember that scene.

169
00:13:05,380 --> 00:13:06,890
Flames as far as the eye could see.

170
00:13:06,890 --> 00:13:08,770
The pervasive stench of death.

171
00:13:08,770 --> 00:13:11,190
Wishing for help when all hope was lost.

172
00:13:11,190 --> 00:13:13,280
What I felt when that wish was granted.

173
00:13:13,820 --> 00:13:19,530
The look of relief on Emiya Kiritsugu's face when he saved me.

174
00:13:19,530 --> 00:13:22,110
That is where you began.

175
00:13:22,110 --> 00:13:26,040
Your gratitude for being saved was nothing but an afterthought.

176
00:13:26,850 --> 00:13:29,820
You simply admired Emiya Kiritsugu.

177
00:13:30,540 --> 00:13:35,640
Because he looked so happy when he saved you,

178
00:13:35,640 --> 00:13:38,300
you were convinced that you wanted the same thing.

179
00:13:39,110 --> 00:13:39,960
He's right.

180
00:13:40,610 --> 00:13:43,310
I wasn't the one who was saved that day.

181
00:13:43,660 --> 00:13:46,560
A huge fire without a single survivor.

182
00:13:46,560 --> 00:13:48,730
A child who should have been beyond saving.

183
00:13:48,730 --> 00:13:51,820
A man who found an impossible survivor.

184
00:13:52,280 --> 00:13:56,090
If you were to ask me which was the real miracle, it'd be...

185
00:13:56,920 --> 00:14:00,230
It's only natural for children to idolize their parents.

186
00:14:00,230 --> 00:14:04,080
But what he left you when he died was a curse.

187
00:14:04,970 --> 00:14:10,080
From that moment, you had no choice but to become a champion of justice.

188
00:14:10,810 --> 00:14:13,430
Your ideals are second-hand.

189
00:14:14,130 --> 00:14:17,480
Ideals that Emiya Kiritsugu failed to live up to.

190
00:14:17,480 --> 00:14:22,060
You're just copying what he believed was right.

191
00:14:22,630 --> 00:14:24,140
That's not...

192
00:14:24,490 --> 00:14:26,300
A champion of justice?

193
00:14:26,910 --> 00:14:28,190
Don't make me laugh.

194
00:14:28,740 --> 00:14:33,650
All your talk of wanting to help others

195
00:14:33,930 --> 00:14:36,740
wasn't something you decided yourself.

196
00:14:37,150 --> 00:14:40,360
Someone like you thinking that he could save anyone...

197
00:14:41,220 --> 00:14:43,600
That's the height of hubris!

198
00:14:50,040 --> 00:14:51,650
That's right.

199
00:14:51,650 --> 00:14:55,710
I admired his wish to help others because it was so beautiful!

200
00:14:56,200 --> 00:15:00,260
Consequently, I had no emotions of my own!

201
00:15:01,680 --> 00:15:04,810
If that isn't hypocrisy, what is?

202
00:15:05,450 --> 00:15:10,860
Driven by my obsession with helping others,
I strove toward that goal,

203
00:15:10,860 --> 00:15:12,730
fully aware that it was the height of arrogance!

204
00:15:13,560 --> 00:15:14,440
Shirou!

205
00:15:15,240 --> 00:15:17,630
But in the end, a fake's a fake.

206
00:15:17,630 --> 00:15:20,060
Hypocrisy like that can't save anyone.

207
00:15:20,060 --> 00:15:23,950
No... You won't even know what you ought to save.

208
00:15:23,950 --> 00:15:26,830
Look! This is the result!

209
00:15:27,290 --> 00:15:31,230
Know that an embodiment of cruel justice that never knew how to save—

210
00:15:31,230 --> 00:15:33,710
never had anything to save—

211
00:15:33,710 --> 00:15:35,550
is what you will ultimately become!

212
00:15:38,400 --> 00:15:41,210
Your ideals are bankrupt.

213
00:15:41,210 --> 00:15:44,730
The idea that others are more important than yourself—

214
00:15:44,730 --> 00:15:47,370
the wish for universal happiness—

215
00:15:47,370 --> 00:15:49,630
is just a fanciful fairytale.

216
00:15:49,630 --> 00:15:52,140
If clinging to that dream is the only way you can live,

217
00:15:52,650 --> 00:15:54,900
then let those ideals drag you to your death!

218
00:16:02,680 --> 00:16:06,410
Most of what he said was right.

219
00:16:07,820 --> 00:16:11,310
But I felt like he was forgetting something important.

220
00:16:19,380 --> 00:16:21,840
I saw Hell.

221
00:16:23,270 --> 00:16:24,970
I saw Hell.

222
00:16:26,460 --> 00:16:28,470
I saw Hell.

223
00:16:29,730 --> 00:16:33,100
I saw a hell that I would go through someday.

224
00:16:35,950 --> 00:16:38,040
You were... Well...

225
00:16:38,860 --> 00:16:40,170
I guess you were right.

226
00:16:43,040 --> 00:16:45,620
Maybe I could have handled things better.

227
00:16:47,930 --> 00:16:50,640
You seem to have lost many things.

228
00:16:51,640 --> 00:16:53,250
You have it wrong.

229
00:16:54,050 --> 00:16:58,980
I'm here because I was stubbornly intent on losing nothing.

230
00:16:59,660 --> 00:17:01,880
I didn't lose anything.

231
00:17:03,620 --> 00:17:04,520
But...

232
00:17:05,510 --> 00:17:07,340
Yes, there is one thing.

233
